[{:db/id "q-37633/selection/899617056192d1022bfac5cf0d82bc941a5f88c83e5b1243a2de3a4bb0f2ed11" :answer/id #uuid "793349a3-14e1-5bde-ae92-cb88d946180d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37633/selection/142bd5071c112b26b648fff75ad587ac55f88aaf316243c4090e7b46cb78b6e2" :answer/id #uuid "ba32fd11-6da9-501e-a2d9-85de306160b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37633/selection/2caf8873a0b6230d1da4479e09489513e971f6209e4cc0bf9afd97773ef077b2" :answer/id #uuid "4feddca6-5376-5c7a-a476-c66a930662bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ is not diagonalizable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37633/selection/60dd8adab7710ba6d8d4f722c3d4b1e159712baa09d78b56abd178a8243b23d8" :answer/id #uuid "23c2a8a5-6898-5a4b-b709-8b8c7b090341" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37633/selection/7a834c0309a4a41915541ad01f284bffc09fb0bd57161b01cd0b42e03c2513d6" :answer/id #uuid "bfb82560-b42c-5520-8c60-98a9a34de52f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37633/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e607a58-c096-5640-8687-a2892d9455d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37633/selection/60dd8adab7710ba6d8d4f722c3d4b1e159712baa09d78b56abd178a8243b23d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-37633/selection/899617056192d1022bfac5cf0d82bc941a5f88c83e5b1243a2de3a4bb0f2ed11" "q-37633/selection/142bd5071c112b26b648fff75ad587ac55f88aaf316243c4090e7b46cb78b6e2" "q-37633/selection/2caf8873a0b6230d1da4479e09489513e971f6209e4cc0bf9afd97773ef077b2" "q-37633/selection/60dd8adab7710ba6d8d4f722c3d4b1e159712baa09d78b56abd178a8243b23d8" "q-37633/selection/7a834c0309a4a41915541ad01f284bffc09fb0bd57161b01cd0b42e03c2513d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37633" :question/id #uuid "a4b19937-90d1-5717-b7a0-7b53ad9d3dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-37633" :question/problem "Given the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]$,\nfind a diagonal matrix $D$ and an invertible matrix $P$ such that $D={P}^{-1}BP.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.**  We need to find the eigenvalues of the matrix. Since matrix $A$ is triangular, its eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal: \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}=7\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-5$\n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $B.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=7,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-7I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $2$nd one). Thus, ${x}_{1}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=0.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=1,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-(-5)I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a homogeneous system of linear equations with the matrix as above. Note, the matrix is already in row echelon form. There is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37633/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ff6446e-7913-5d55-adfd-124649f3f1c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37633"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140045/selection/8d3ead34b05b68ebe304431ed3352d757bb09edae97fd3c213bb4d005fa97aa3" :answer/id #uuid "e93a9c55-8fec-550d-808f-afd03f26d3cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140045/selection/83e1afda14b7828dd32335bb4b02d9e461e6f35eda76b7346cb6b7a1789f445c" :answer/id #uuid "a850083c-117b-59f3-ba15-6d5a442d2621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140045/selection/51a095e0b68bf5e4f23f4ce05cd97d0463c784481999fd29715f89caae21911b" :answer/id #uuid "9c2c83b5-ac91-57a3-ac6c-76f0fbbdbbe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140045/selection/655ede254939c8720ff15fa47ebfaa58a37f5de0c0b757a45cc6bf14b9606903" :answer/id #uuid "28850b83-c4b0-57bb-8209-a7274e569b86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140045/selection/a58e880e036264e5b21442a2e9867416c984cde73a96371bb168dcb66090a333" :answer/id #uuid "b9f5a770-68f5-5722-8f61-48518553a391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140045/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "484e247f-cdf6-58ee-b821-37819ce89d49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140045/selection/a58e880e036264e5b21442a2e9867416c984cde73a96371bb168dcb66090a333" :answer-field/choices ["q-140045/selection/8d3ead34b05b68ebe304431ed3352d757bb09edae97fd3c213bb4d005fa97aa3" "q-140045/selection/83e1afda14b7828dd32335bb4b02d9e461e6f35eda76b7346cb6b7a1789f445c" "q-140045/selection/51a095e0b68bf5e4f23f4ce05cd97d0463c784481999fd29715f89caae21911b" "q-140045/selection/655ede254939c8720ff15fa47ebfaa58a37f5de0c0b757a45cc6bf14b9606903" "q-140045/selection/a58e880e036264e5b21442a2e9867416c984cde73a96371bb168dcb66090a333"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140045" :question/id #uuid "16966b44-d262-59a2-bf48-8567403d396f" :question/math-academy-id "q-140045" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 \\\\ ∗ & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $A=PD{P}^{-1},$ find the first column of the matrix $P.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagonal matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]$, we deduce that the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4.$\n\nSo, the first column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=3.$ \n\nNow, we simply need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{1}=3.$ Computing $A-3I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-3I & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $P=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140045/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca18fa52-5494-53ad-bd02-208aba4ff9e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140045"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
